# Web files

- Semantic HTML, few IDs. Classes are for CSS; `data-widget` for JS.
- CSS variables on `:root` for coral, periwinkle, magenta, surfaces, borders. No magic hex scattered in JS except the colour widget’s palette array.
- Grid and full-screen are CSS (`grid-template`, `.widget.is-full`). JS toggles a class and updates `layout.order`.
- Native dialogs: `<dialog>` or one overlay component — consistent padding, radius, buttons.
- ES modules (`type="module"`). No globals except what `index.html` must boot.
- Widgets **keep running** when shrunk: do not `clearInterval` on contract.

```css
/* ✅ widget size is CSS, not JS measuring the window */
.board { display: grid; gap: var(--gap); min-height: 100dvh; }
.board[data-n="4"] { grid-template: 1fr 1fr / 1fr 1fr; }
.widget.is-full { position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 5; }
```
